 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "• Full stop (.): ends a statement.  • Question mark (?): ends a question.  • Exclamation mark (!): shows strong feeling.\n• Comma (,): separates items in a list (“drums, flutes and guitars”), after an introductory word (“However, …”), and before direct speech.\n• Apostrophe ('): shows possession (Tabe's guitar, the actors' costumes) or a missing letter (don't, it's = it is).\n• Quotation marks (“ ”): enclose the exact words spoken: She said, “The film starts at eight.”\n• Colon (:): introduces a list or an explanation.  • Capital letters: at the start of a sentence, for names, places, days, months, titles.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "Punctuate: “tabe asked where is the cinema”",
  "steps": [
   "Capital letters for the start and the name: Tabe.",
   "Direct speech in quotation marks with a comma before it, and a question mark: Tabe asked, “Where is the cinema?”"
  ],
  "answer": "Tabe asked, “Where is the cinema?”",
  "checks": []
 },
